\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. A branch so fair has blossom'd
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 From tender parent stem;
\par Out of the root of Jesse
\par As told by godly men
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And brought a flow'r so bright,
\par Well in the midst of winter
\par When half spent was the night.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   This little Rose so lovely
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Of which Isaiah tells
\par Was brought to us by Mary
\par The maid whom God loved well
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par By His decree and pow'r
\par A holy child she bore us,
\par Well at the midnight hour.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  This little flow'r so fragrant
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  My heart fills with delight,
\par  For with its shining splendor
\par  It drives away the night
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord Jesus, God's own son
\par  Save us from sin and sorrow
\par \pard       Till heaven we have won!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

